{
  "about": "Source reads over a row's collected records and over ODM inputs (LOOKUP-8, COLUMN-2, NAME-9 to NAME-11). A filtered source, a mapping's source and a first_available's sources read their own row's collected records; a selected record without a value never takes an unselected record's value; a conflict counts the values its filter keeps; a filter cannot read another relation; equal dates are one value and distinct ones are counted; an ODM input reports its first record without a subject key and how many lack one; and a column odm read takes the ODM scope of the row template that built its row, also when an ODM input other than the base drives that template. Moved from execution_retired_odm_context.rs, its retired_odm_context module. A test that saved is a save case with the bytes it compared, a test that read the run's issues compared them whole, and the handler counts one test compared whole are the report's handler rows at SPEC_PATH, NAME and COUNT. Every value is its test's.",
  "documents": {
    "odm_value": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [SubjectKey]\ninput: {ODM: odm.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [SubjectKey, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: SubjectKey, type: str, derivation: ODM.SubjectKey}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: str, derivation: ODM.Value}\n",
    "odm_target": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [GroupID]\ninput: {ODM: odm.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [GroupID, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: GroupID, type: str, derivation: ODM.GroupID}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: str, derivation: {source: {variable: ODM.Value, filter: \"ODM.RecordKind = 'TARGET'\"}}}\n",
    "odm_date": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [SubjectKey]\ninput: {ODM: {path: odm.csv, types: {VISITDT: date}}}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [SubjectKey, VALUE]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: SubjectKey, type: str, derivation: ODM.SubjectKey}\n  - {name: VALUE, type: date, derivation: ODM.VISITDT}\n",
    "odm_driver": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [ID, SEQ]\nbase: BASE\ninput: {BASE: base.csv, SRC: odm.csv}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, SEQ, VAL]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str}\n  - {name: SEQ, type: int, derivation: {row_number: {window: {order_by: [ID]}}}}\n  - {name: VAL, type: str, derivation: {odm: SRC.IT.TEST.OID}}\nrows:\n  - id: occurrence\n    dataset: SRC\n    filter: \"SRC.ItemOID = 'IT.ANCHOR'\"\n    derivations: {ID: \"'one'\"}\n",
    "items": "StudyOID,SubjectKey,ItemOID,Value\nS1,001,IT.DM.SEX,Male\nS1,001,IT.DM.AGE,34\nS1,001,IT.DM.ARM,Placebo\n",
    "visit_dates": "StudyOID,SubjectKey,VISITDT,ItemOID,Value\nS1,001,2025-01-02,IT.A,a\nS1,001,2025-01-02,IT.B,b\n",
    "occurrences": "StudyOID,MetaDataVersionOID,SubjectKey,StudyEventOID,StudyEventRepeatKey,FormOID,FormRepeatKey,ItemGroupOID,ItemGroupRepeatKey,ItemOID,Value\nS,M,P,E,,F,,G,,IT.ANCHOR,anchor\nS,M,P,E,,F,,G,,IT.TEST.OID,Y\n"
  },
